  "status_text": "Three contributor proofs were accepted by Lean within two minutes just after 17:00 UTC (L-meta-25512, L-meta-25565, L-meta-25930). The third says: under a stated condition on how often a table repeats its rows and columns, a circuit with NOT gates for it can be replaced by one without them of at most the same size, when one row and one column are selected and gates read at most two wires. And in house, 79 minutes after it was filed, Lean checked that every circuit for one three-by-three matching question can be put, without growing, in a form whose opening gate is one of five (L-meta-25876).",
